    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-03",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A nucleated pattern concentrates dwellings near one another. A crossroads, shared service, suitable site, security arrangement or historical decision can help explain a cluster where the evidence supports it. The cluster can reduce some distances between households and shared facilities, while fields or workplaces may lie farther away. Nucleation does not by itself establish a large town, a high income or one particular political history.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-2",
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-01-2",
