    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-04",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A linear pattern extends along a line such as a road, river margin, valley floor or other accessible strip. The visible alignment should be stated before its cause is inferred. Houses along a road may reflect access; those beside a valley route may also reflect relief or available land. A line of houses on a map is evidence of shape, not proof that each resident uses river water or works on the road.",
      "claim_ids": [
