    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-05",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A teaching plan can use identical house symbols in three panels with the same orientation and scale. Panel A places eight houses apart across farm plots; B places eight along one east–west route; C groups eight around a crossroads. Keeping the count equal shows that the difference is arrangement rather than total houses.\n\n![Dispersed, linear and nucleated settlement panels at one scale](../../assets/images/ITEM-6137-3.3-002-INTERP-answer.png)",
      "claim_ids": [
