    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-06",
      "block_type": "worked_application",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "To describe the panels, use spacing, alignment and concentration. A is scattered with intervening land, B forms an elongated route-related arrangement and C has a compact cluster. An answer saying only that all panels contain houses does not describe the distinguishing pattern. If a resource includes a scale, distances can support the comparison; without it, avoid invented spacing in metres.",
