    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-09",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A settlement can change as new dwellings are added. Growth along an access road can create a linear extension around an older nucleus, while new farm plots can support more scattered homes. Comparing dated maps helps establish the change. A single present map cannot prove the sequence or the reason for it. Distinguish the current form from a historical explanation.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-2",
