    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-11",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A geographical explanation links the pattern to physical and human evidence. A narrow accessible valley, a shared water point or a planned village can each influence arrangement through different processes. The relevant factor should be visible or supplied in an accompanying record. Shape alone cannot establish an exact history of land rights, household income or government policy.",
