    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-12",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "Settlement size and pattern should be described separately. Two panels can each contain eight house symbols, with one scattered and one clustered. The count is equal, while the arrangement differs. Another panel may have more houses yet remain dispersed across a larger area. A pattern classification should therefore use spacing relative to the mapped area, not simply the largest number of symbols.",
