    {
      "block_id": "BL-6137-3.3.01-14",
      "block_type": "plain_explanation",
      "heading": "",
      "text": "A nucleus can be irregular rather than circular. Houses may cluster around a junction or service without equal spacing or a neat outline. Likewise, dispersed farmsteads need not be arranged randomly: each can occupy a deliberate position on a holding. These details help interpret realistic maps, where the three ideal shapes are often modified by terrain and history.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-1",
        "CL-6137-3.3.01-2",
